IDEA OF THE DAY

Permit expediting for residential solar installers.

The problem: a residential solar installer waits an average of 4-7 weeks for a
local building permit, and the paperwork differs in every one of the 3,000+
jurisdictions in the US. Installers describe permitting as the single largest
source of delay between a signed contract and a paid install.

Why now: several states have mandated automated permitting review for
residential solar, but adoption at the county level is slow and uneven.

The business: a service that files, tracks and chases permits on behalf of
installers, priced per permit. Installers already pay staff to do this badly.

Signals: r/solar has recurring threads about permit delays. Two incumbents
exist, both focused on enterprise installers.

